{{!-- ONE bulk-read choice, priced for this account (web.js pricedChoices): "how far back?" (partials/history-choice.hbs)
      and the follow reconciler (views/follows-back.hbs). Either a button that POSTs `key` to `action`, or (`pick`: a
      form's id, the start page's Get started) a radio in that form, before its label so CSS can mark the picked one
      without :has() (iOS Safari doesn't re-check it). One the balance doesn't cover can't be chosen (the route refuses
      it too), and beside it the ONE top-up that covers it (`topup`, billing.topupFor): a LINK, since Checkout is
      off-site and the CSP's form-action 'self' would block a form leading there; paid, the page comes back with it
      choosable. Context: a choice ({ key, label, price, affordable, topup, detail, selected }); hash: action | pick,
      back (where the top-up returns), detail (when the choice has none). --}}
{{#*inline "option-body"}}<span class="option-head"><span class="option-label">{{label}}</span><span class="option-cost">{{cost price}}</span></span>{{#if detail}}<span class="option-detail">{{detail}}</span>{{/if}}{{/inline}}
<div class="option-row">
  {{#if pick}}
    <input class="option-radio" type="radio" id="option-{{key}}" name="key" value="{{key}}" form="{{pick}}"{{#if selected}} checked{{/if}}{{#unless affordable}} disabled{{/unless}}>
    <label class="option" for="option-{{key}}">{{> option-body}}</label>
  {{else}}
    <form method="post" action="{{action}}" data-busy>
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{@root.csrfToken}}">
      <input type="hidden" name="key" value="{{key}}">
      <button type="submit" class="option"{{#unless affordable}} disabled{{/unless}}>{{> option-body}}</button>
    </form>
  {{/if}}
  {{#if topup}}{{#if @root.funds.payable}}<a class="pill option-add" href="/billing/topup?amount={{topup}}&amp;back={{back}}">Add ${{topup}} for this</a>{{/if}}{{/if}}
</div>
